| PC networking: PCNE2 gives the PC an NE2000, and PCNAT puts it on the
| Internet through RISC OS (a NAT, so RISC OS keeps its own address).
| PCNE2 reads its NE2000Basic and NE2000Advanced options from the PC
| configuration (-F): -pTCPIP for TCP/IP.  It uses PCNAT unless
| Diva$SuggestedInterface or a -D option names another network interface.
RMEnsure PCNAT 0.01 RMLoad <Obey$Dir>.PCNAT
RMEnsure PCNAT 0.01 Error <Obey$Dir>.PCNAT not found or too old
If "<Diva$SuggestedInterface>" = "" Then Set Diva$SuggestedInterface pcnat0
RMEnsure PCNE2 2.15 RMLoad <Obey$Dir>.PCNE2 -F
RMEnsure PCNE2 2.15 Error <Obey$Dir>.PCNE2 not found or too old
